	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Accès Postgres depuis autre PC]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=28596#p28596"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,</p><p>Vous pouvez essayer de remplacer toutes vos lignes du pg_hba.conf par ceci (et relancer l&#039;instance) :</p><p>#connexion socket unix :<br />local&#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; md5<br />#connexion TCP/IP ipv4 :<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;192.168.1.33/32&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; md5<br />#connexion TCP/IP ipv6 :<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; md5<br />host&#160; &#160; replication&#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; md5<br />host&#160; &#160; replication&#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;md5</p><p>(dans cet ordre)</p>]]></content>
